    qa: [
      { q: 'What does the example of the patient gardener show?', choices: ['A patient person should avoid taking any action at all.', 'Growth can be forced if one works hard enough.', 'Genuine patience goes together with steady, continuing effort.', 'Patience means waiting for problems to solve themselves.'], answer: 2, why: '第4段落：庭師は水をやり害虫から守りながら、成長は急がせられないと受け入れる。本当の忍耐は粘り強い努力と両立する。' },
      { q: 'Why might modern life make patience harder to cultivate?', choices: ['Because many desires can now be fulfilled at once.', 'Because modern life requires long periods of waiting.', 'Because people now practice waiting calmly too often.', 'Because technology makes learning instruments much slower.'], answer: 0, why: '第6段落：多くの願いがすぐにかなうので、ふつうの遅れが耐えがたく感じられ、待つ習慣が弱まるかもしれない。' },
    ],
