    qa: [
      { q: 'Why, according to the writer, are digital accounts hard to handle under inheritance rules?', choices: ['Accounts are worth much less than land or money.', 'Companies always delete accounts after their users die.', 'Users typically hold permission rather than ownership.', 'Relatives rarely wish to read the messages inside.'], answer: 2, why: '第5段落 users usually do not own them but merely have permission to use a service。相続のきまりは所有する財産を前提としている。' },
      { q: 'What can be inferred about critics of programs that imitate the dead?', choices: ['They believe such programs cost families too much.', 'They doubt that grieving people would ever use them.', 'They want companies to record more people\'s voices.', 'They think healthy grieving and consent are at risk.'], answer: 3, why: '第6段落。批判する人々は、死を受け入れられなくなること（健全な悲しみの過程）と、本人の同意なく声を再現することを問題にしている。' },
    ],
