    qa: [
      { q: 'Why do the whiskers of a swimming seal stay quiet in calm water?', choices: ['Their flattened, wavy shape reduces the seal\'s own vibrations.', 'The seal holds its whiskers flat against its face while swimming.', 'Their many nerve fibres are switched off until prey appears nearby.', 'Calm water contains no movements that a whisker could detect.'], answer: 0, why: '第4段落で、平たく波打った形がアザラシ自身の動きによる振動を大きく減らすと述べている。' },
      { q: 'Why are engineers interested in the whiskers of harbour seals?', choices: ['They hope to train seals to inspect harbours and pipelines.', 'They want cameras that work better at night under the ice.', 'Artificial whiskers could help robots sense currents in murky water.', 'Seal whiskers could be used to make stronger underwater cables.'], answer: 2, why: '第6段落で、カメラが役に立たない濁った水の中で、流れや航跡を感じとるために、アザラシのひげをまねた人工のひげを設計し始めていると述べている。' },
    ],
